# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Private working material — never in the public repo
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Phase plans, launch runbook, opsec notes, tracker.
# The public audit trail is the site and the published epoch snapshots.
docs/
HANDOFF.md
x-post.md
*-DRAFT.md
*.private.md
notes/
private/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets and keys — the ones that end projects
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Solana keypairs are plain JSON byte arrays with no distinguishing
# extension, so match on name as well as on location.
*keypair*.json
id.json
wallet*.json
**/deploy/*.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
site/config.local.js
secrets/
.secrets/
*.secret

# pump.fun session tokens used to read the callout feed.
# These authenticate as a real account — treat them like a key.
.callout-auth
callout-token*

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Epoch working files
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Published snapshots live in snapshots/ and MUST be committed —
# they are the audit trail. Scratch output does not.
epochs/scratch/
*.snapshot.tmp
# The hourly poll's rolling memory. Working state between polls — every epoch's
# raw capture is committed under snapshots/, which is the record that matters.
epochs/callout-store.json
# The devnet dry run: its manifest, its throwaway keys, its fabricated callout
# store and its snapshots. None of it is evidence of anything and a fake epoch
# in the audit trail is worse than no audit trail.
epochs/devnet/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build output and dependencies
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
target/
.anchor/
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.bin/
*.so
# package-lock.json is COMMITTED, for the same reason Cargo.lock is: the scripts
# it pins hold the snapshot key in memory and sign with it, so their dependency
# versions have to be as fixed as the deployed binary's. `npm ci` in the runbook
# requires it. yarn/pnpm are not used here.
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local validator and test state
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
test-ledger/
.ledger/
*.log

# Claude Code's local permission state. Machine-specific, and it records
# absolute paths from whoever ran it — including directories that have nothing
# to do with this project. `.claude/launch.json` IS committed: it is generic and
# it is how the dev server gets started.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editor and OS noise
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# History backups — must never be committed
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.bundle
